  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to decrease the illegal trade of tiger and rhino horn specimens throughout the Mekong region of Southeast Asia. This will be done by: (1) increasing information sharing between the governments of Thailand, Cambodia, Vietnam, Lao PDR and China with regards to rhino horn and tiger trade routes, suspect profiles, and specific smuggling methods at specific border.crossings; and (2) improving performance of Thai, Vietnamese, Cambodian, Lao PDR and Chinese law enforcement officers in identifying and arresting high-level tiger and rhino horn traffickers...Specifically this will be done by: (1) facilitating bilateral and multilateral Special Investigation Group meetings that enable information sharing, joint training and planning among key rhino and tiger source, transit and consumer countries in the Mekong region; (2) training and equipping investigators to pursue cases and develop regional enforcement capacity; (3) providing on-the-ground training, mentoring and tip-off support, where requested, to government investigators (only in Thailand, not in Vietnam, China, Cambodia or Lao PDR); and (4) following major cases until their successful conclusion..&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
